3. FT8 specifications referred to (no source code copied, to the best of the author's knowledge)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

main/index.html contains an FT8 decoder written for this project. Protocol constants and
tables (LDPC(174,91) parity-check matrices, CRC-14 polynomial, Gray code mapping, Costas
array, 77-bit message format) are the published specification values taken from:

  - ft8_lib by Karlis Goba (YL3JG)  https://github.com/kgoba/ft8_lib   (MIT License)
  - WSJT-X by Joe Taylor (K1JT) et al.  https://wsjt.sourceforge.io/   (GNU GPL v3)

To the best of the author's knowledge no source code of these projects was copied, but
similarity of the constants and tables is unavoidable because they must match the
specification exactly.

Phase 4 TX uses the MIT-licensed ft8_lib encoder and message packer from upstream commit
9fec6ca39886edbf96f4f5e71edc76da5074e871 in components/ft8_lib. See its LICENSE for the full terms.
The GFSK timing and pulse-shaping reference is Eugen Trifu YO9VA's ftx1-pult
(https://github.com/Eugen68/ftx1-pult), server/ft8.py.


4. Map data
-----------

main/map.html contains coastline data derived from Natural Earth 50m land
(public domain, https://www.naturalearthdata.com/), simplified to 0.02 degrees.
